{"step_index":56,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:56:39Z","thinking":"**Seeking a Counterexample**\n\nThe inequality $\\gamma_t(G) \\le \\gamma_R(G)$ isn't universal; need an explicit counterexample. The search didn't yield results up to a graph size of 7, so the search space needs expansion. Consider graphs with 8 nodes, or specific graph families, that may possess the desired property. The goal is to identify a graph exhibiting large total domination but small Roman domination.\n\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\nimport networkx as nx\nimport itertools\nimport random\n\ndef total_domination_number(G):\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\n    n = len(nodes)\n    adj = {u: set(G.neighbors(u)) for u in nodes}\n    if any(len(adj[u]) == 0 for u in nodes):\n        return None\n    for k in range(1, n + 1):\n        for S in itertools.combinations(nodes, k):\n            S_set = set(S)\n            if all(adj[v] & S_set for v in nodes):\n                return k\n    return 0\n\ndef roman_domination_number(G):\n    # Using integer programming or greedy/branch-and-bound for speed\n    import scipy.optimize\n    # or simple ILP using scipy.optimize.milp\n    # minimize sum(f_v) = sum(x_v + 2*y_v)\n    # s.t. x_v + y_v + sum_{u in N(v)} y_u >= 1 for all v\n    # x_v + y_v <= 1\n    # x_v, y_v in {0, 1}\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\n    n = len(nodes)\n    import numpy as np\n    # 2*n variables: x_0..x_{n-1}, y_0..y_{n-1}\n    c = np.array([1]*n + [2]*n)\n    # constraints:\n    # 1) x_v + y_v + sum_{u in N(v)} y_u >= 1  => -x_v - y_v - sum y_u <= -1\n    # 2) x_v + y_v <= 1\n    A_rows = []\n    b_l = []\n    b_u = []\n    for i, v in enumerate(nodes):\n        row = [0]*(2*n)\n        row[i] = 1 # x_v\n        row[n + i] = 1 # y_v\n        for u in G.neighbors(v):\n            j = nodes.index(u)\n            row[n + j] = 1 # y_u\n        A_rows.append(row)\n        b_l.append(1)\n        b_u.append(np.inf)\n    for i in range(n):\n        row = [0]*(2*n)\n        row[i] = 1\n        row[n + i] = 1\n        A_rows.append(row)\n        b_l.append(0)\n        b_u.append(1)\n    \n    constraints = scipy.optimize.LinearConstraint(A_rows, b_l, b_u)\n    integrality = np.ones(2*n)\n    bounds = scipy.optimize.Bounds(0, 1)\n    res = scipy.optimize.milp(c=c, constraints=constraints, integrality=integrality, bounds=bounds)\n    return int(round(res.fun))\n\n# Fast ILP for total domination number:\ndef fast_total_dom(G):\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\n    n = len(nodes)\n    if any(G.degree(v) == 0 for v in nodes):\n        return None\n    import numpy as np\n    import scipy.optimize\n    c = np.ones(n)\n    A_rows = []\n    b_l = []\n    b_u = []\n    for v in nodes:\n        row = [0]*n\n        for u in G.neighbors(v):\n            row[nodes.index(u)] = 1\n        A_rows.append(row)\n        b_l.append(1)\n        b_u.append(np.inf)\n    constraints = scipy.optimize.LinearConstraint(A_rows, b_l, b_u)\n    integrality = np.ones(n)\n    bounds = scipy.optimize.Bounds(0, 1)\n    res = scipy.optimize.milp(c=c, constraints=constraints, integrality=integrality, bounds=bounds)\n    return int(round(res.fun))\n\n# Test trees up to order 12\nprint(\"Testing trees...\")\nfor n in range(2, 14):\n    for T in nx.generators.nonisomorphic_trees(n):\n        td = fast_total_dom(T)\n        rd = roman_domination_number(T)\n        if td > rd:\n            print(f\"FOUND COUNTEREXAMPLE IN TREES! n={n}, edges={list(T.edges())}, td={td}, rd={rd}\")\n            exit(0)\nprint(\"No counterexample among trees up to 13.\")\n'","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Testing trees up to order 13","toolSummary":"Test trees for counterexample"}}]}
