{"step_index":91,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:58:03Z","thinking":"**Deriving Roman Domination Weight**\n\nThe logic hinges on finding a valid Roman dominating function. Given *any* set V2, the uncovered vertices—those not dominated by V2—are precisely V excluding the union of V2 and its neighbors. If the number of these uncovered vertices is small enough, selecting them (or any superset) as V1 results in a Roman dominating function with weight 2|V2| + |V1|, which is less than a target threshold.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"which geng || find / -name geng 2>/dev/null","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Checking for geng","toolSummary":"Find geng binary"}}]}
